{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a5455b56-22f1-4bf6-b577-813a5fdf1c3d","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Target File \u0026 Symbols\n- **Target File**: [date_range.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-001_23288_1795228521439_icm_lite/date_range.py)\n- **Inspected Symbols**: `_parse_date`, `generate_date_range` (and `test_basic_progression` in [test_visible.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-001_23288_1795228521439_icm_lite/tests/test_visible.py))\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n1. **Inclusive start, exclusive end**: Returns `YYYY-MM-DD` strings starting at `start_date` and stopping strictly before `end_date` (`current \u003c end`).\n2. **Equal boundary**: Returns `[]` when `start_date == end_date`.\n3. **Single-day \u0026 multi-day transitions**: Correctly handles consecutive days, month/year boundaries, and leap years.\n4. **Reversed range**: Raises `ValueError(\"start_date must not be after end_date\")` when `start_date \u003e end_date`.\n5. **Invalid inputs**: Enforces strict 10-character `YYYY-MM-DD` strings or `datetime.date` instances (excluding `datetime.datetime`), raising `ValueError(\"Invalid date format, expected YYYY-MM-DD\")` on failure.\n6. **Step validation**: Raises `ValueError(\"step_days must be a positive integer\")` when `step_days \u003c= 0` or is not a positive `int`.\n\n### Changes Applied\n- Updated [`_parse_date`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-001_23288_1795228521439_icm_lite/date_range.py#L8-L18) to validate input type and 10-character `YYYY-MM-DD` format, raising `ValueError(\"Invalid date format, expected YYYY-MM-DD\")` on invalid strings or `datetime` objects.\n- Updated [`generate_date_range`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/tmp/disposable_workspaces/live_BENCH-001_23288_1795228521439_icm_lite/date_range.py#L21-L46) to validate `step_days \u003e 0`, check `start \u003e end`, and change the loop condition from `while current \u003c= end:` to `while current \u003c end:`.\n\n### Verification \u0026 Remaining Risk\n- **Automated Checks** (via `filter_output.py`):\n  - `✓ Command succeeded: python -m pytest`\n  - `✓ Command succeeded: python -c ...` (verified equal boundary, single-day range, year/leap-year transitions, step progression, reversed ranges, invalid date formats, and non-positive `step_days`).\n- **Remaining Risk**: Minimal. Note that `datetime.datetime` (which is a subclass of `datetime.date` in Python) is explicitly rejected in `_parse_date` to strictly honor the `str | datetime.date` contract; if callers pass `datetime.datetime` objects expecting implicit `.date()` coercion, it will raise `ValueError`.\n","duration_seconds":63.1116643,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":41470,"output_tokens":3352,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":148218,"total_tokens":44822}}}
